 "blocks": [
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "Using state-of-being clauses as adjectives"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 4,
   "text": "Vocabulary"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "1. 国際【こく・さい】- international"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "2. 教育【きょう・いく】- education"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "3. センター- center"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "4. 登場【とう・じょう】- entry (on stage)"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "5. 人物【じん・ぶつ】- character"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "6. 立入【たち・いり】- entering"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "7. 禁止【きん・し】- prohibition, ban"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "8. 学生【がく・せい】- student"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "9. 人【ひと】- person"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "10. 学校【がっ・こう】- school"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "11. 行く【い・く】(u-verb) - to go"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "12. 子供【こ・ども】- child"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "13. 立派【りっ・ぱ】(na-adj) - fine, elegant"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "14. 大人【おとな】- adult"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "15. なる (u-verb) - to become"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "16. 友達【とも・だち】- friend"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "17. いい (i-adj) - good"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "18. 先週【せん・しゅう】- last week"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "19. 医者【い・しゃ】- doctor"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "20. 仕事【し・ごと】- job"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "21. 辞める【や・める】(ru-verb) - to quit"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "The negative, past, and negative past conjugations of verbs can be used just like adjectives to directly modify nouns. However, we cannot do this with the plain non-past state-of-being using 「だ」 . (I told you this was a pain in the butt.) The language has particles for this purpose, which will be covered in the next section."
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 4,
   "text": "Note"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "You cannot use 「だ」 to directly modify a noun with a noun like you can with 「だった」、「じゃ ない」、and 「じゃなかった」."
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "You can, however, have a string of nouns placed together when they're not meant to modify each other."
  }
 ]
}